{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790960017,"nonce":"RBNrv1THKMsDIXGEXln+uRfnWEk=","title":"Lua host: open_host lowers and compiles the Lua runtime library in every process","message":"zyntax_lua::open_host (the embedding entry caribou uses) runs TieredRuntime::compile_typed_program / lower_typed_program over the Lua runtime library each time a host starts, and zyntax_lua_capi::host_state adds to it, before the host loads its first chunk. Caribou's gpu plugin fixture (2026-10-02, debug build with zyntax crates at opt-level 3, Time Profiler, main thread): caribou_lua's prepare takes 106 to 154 ms of a roughly 380 ms start-up; about 40 ms more is the host's own helper chunk through lua_load and zlc_pcall.\n\nSame shape as a440a60eb4f132f0069b3d67811822c865810b964da28bbdea2a2a4429556489 (Python's exception prelude lowered for every program) and 507f983a0dd8649ea3be60c1f1bd2e100de93c96f03865f1fa4878b154cd3b40 (ZynML's preludes): ship the Lua library lowered (a snapshot the host links and decodes on demand), or compiled, so open_host only links. Related: b3996333e0fc388014a015ee1310316b66c58fd6b74e735002670ffa5032890b (zylua start-up), a88b2004484711b7d509b977af4827d7b5d1e60753976c4153ba46117a40a800 (whole reachable library compiled up front). Caribou tracks it as its git-bug 8463e3cf49d7278b77faebdb0e1b464cf2420e21f2ee6abf576adb3d0ae8f444.\n\nDone when open_host's cost no longer scales with the library: measure it with a release build on the Mac and the NUC.","files":null}]}